Subject: [PATCH] cpufreq: scmi: enable the Piano boost frequencies by default

Match the board's existing userspace default at driver registration, before
CPU policies are created. Keep firmware OPP classification and the normal
cpufreq thermal and frequency QoS limits; other SCMI boards retain their
existing default.

---
--- a/drivers/cpufreq/scmi-cpufreq.c
+++ b/drivers/cpufreq/scmi-cpufreq.c
@@ -464,6 +464,9 @@
 	}
 #endif
 
+	if (of_machine_is_compatible("xiaomi,piano"))
+		scmi_cpufreq_driver.boost_enabled = true;
+
 	ret = cpufreq_register_driver(&scmi_cpufreq_driver);
 	if (ret) {
 		dev_err(dev, "%s: registering cpufreq failed, err: %d\n",
